Done. All six features are implemented and the official challenge validator passes **EXCELLENT (9/9, score 1.0)**.

**`app/auth.py`** — `require_api_key` now returns 401 when `X-API-Key` is missing or not in `VALID_API_KEYS`, otherwise returns the mapped username (`app/auth.py:8-11`).

**`app/main.py`**:
- `GET /tasks` — optional `status`, `priority`, `assigned_to` filters (combinable), then `page`/`page_size` slicing with defaults 1/20 (`app/main.py:17-31`).
- `POST /tasks` — auth via `Depends(require_api_key)`, 404 if `project_id` not in `projects`, auto-ID as `max(existing id) + 1`, returns 201 with the created task (`app/main.py:37-48`).
- `PUT /tasks/{task_id}` — auth, partial update using `model_dump(exclude_unset=True)` so omitted fields are untouched and explicit `null` still clears `assigned_to`; 404 if missing (`app/main.py:50-60`).
- `DELETE /tasks/{task_id}` — auth, removes from the in-memory list, 204 on success, 404 if missing (`app/main.py:62-69`).

Design note: GET endpoints stay unauthenticated because the existing validator exercises them without headers; auth is scoped to the mutating endpoints as specified. Verified with both a 13-check smoke test (all pass, including combined filters and auth/404 edge cases) and the upstream `challenges/feature/validator.py` run against the workdir.
